    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0753" n="643" xml:id="pg643"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25, 1890</date>.
                        (Received July 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 330.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 257 of the 2d
                    instant, relative to the claim of Howard C. Walker for injuries inflicted
                    (during 1883–’87) by the Mexican authorities at Minatitlan, Vera Cruz, I beg to
                    inclose copy and translation of a note from Mr. Manuel Azpiroz, acting minister
                    of foreign affairs, stating that, pursuant to a report rendered on April 18,
                    1887, by Señor Lic. Bon Ignacio L. Vallarta, a legal adviser of the foreign
                    office, the Mexican Government was not responsible for damages in the
                    premises.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. Ryan.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d378-a1.xml" xpointer="d378-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
